# Accepted vulnerabilities, and the only reason `make scan` and the CI scan job
# do not fail today.
#
# This file is the gate's exit condition. Everything listed here is a finding
# that existed when image scanning was introduced (2026-08-09) and that nobody
# had triaged yet; anything NOT listed here fails the build. So the way to
# close this out is to empty the file, one line at a time, and the way to keep
# it honest is to refuse to add a line without a reason next to it.
#
# Adding an entry is a decision, not a formality. Write why, and what would
# remove it. An entry with no note is a bug.
#
# Check what is still outstanding with:
#   make scan
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go dependencies — controller and authd
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are reachable (govulncheck agrees, not just Trivy), and both are fixed
# by a dependency bump rather than a code change. They were out of scope for
# the change that added scanning. Removing these two lines is the same edit as
# flipping `continue-on-error` off on test.yml's govulncheck step — do all
# three together.
#
# golang.org/x/text v0.37.0 -> v0.39.0 (GO-2026-5970, infinite loop on invalid
# UTF-8). Reached from FrameJobReconciler.Reconcile via norm.Form.
CVE-2026-56852
# google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.0 -> v1.82.1 (GO-2026-6061, xDS RBAC and HTTP/2
# transport). Reached from the Talos client's gRPC transport.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UI image base layer — nginx:alpine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All four are Alpine package CVEs in the nginx:alpine base, not in anything
# Frame writes. They clear when the base image is rebuilt against a newer
# Alpine, so the fix is to pin and bump the base rather than to patch anything
# here — which is also review finding I11 (the UI image is unpinned
# `nginx:alpine` and runs as root). Expect these to disappear with that work.
#
# c-ares 1.34.6-r0 -> 1.34.8-r0
CVE-2026-33630
# curl / libcurl 8.19.0-r0 -> 8.20.0-r0
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276
# libexpat 2.8.1-r0 -> 2.8.2-r0
CVE-2026-56408
